# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference — `scripts/generate-og.mjs` fingerprints its own raw
# bytes into RENDER_DIGEST so that editing the card layout invalidates every
# card. Under Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows that file lands on
# disk with CRLF, the digest no longer matches the one recorded in
# scripts/og-manifest.json on an LF machine, and `npm run verify:assets` reports
# all six cards permanently stale. Regenerating there would bake the CRLF digest
# into the manifest and break the LF machines instead, so the manifest would
# ping-pong on every commit. Pinning eol=lf removes the platform from the hash.
#
# Same reasoning keeps `npm run format:check` honest: Prettier enforces LF, so
# a CRLF checkout fails the check on files nobody touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these, and don't try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
